{"object":"Optical keyboards use emitters and photo sensors, can offer faster response, and avoid physical contact between moving sensing parts. Debouncing addresses contact oscillation that could register multiple keystrokes. These generic mechanisms do not measure the SK61 or K6 end-to-end latency or human perceptibility.","predicate":"are_real_mechanisms_not_product_latency_tests","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Keyboard_technology","subject":"optical sensing and keyboard debouncing","text":"Optical sensing and contact debouncing are physically real mechanisms, but their generic descriptions do not measure either frozen keyboard's total latency or prove a perceptible gaming benefit.","title":"prop_optical_debounce_scope"}